:: Church encounter - love mediation [bg-guesthouse]
<h1 class="ptitle">GUEST HOUSE</h1>
<br /><br />
/* A loving nun helps two guests who are drawn to each other past a rough patch, and encourages them to make up the way lovers do. */
<<set _ce = setup.churchEncounters>>
<<set _fx = setup.nurseryEncounters>>
<<set _cast = _ce.cast()>>
<<if !_cast>>
	<<goto 'Guest house'>>
<<else>>
<<set _nun = _cast.nun, _a = _cast.first, _b = _cast.second>>
<<set _nunName = setup.displayName(_nun), _aName = setup.displayName(_a), _bName = setup.displayName(_b)>>
<<set _nHe = setup.pronounceWhat(_nun), _nHis = setup.pronounceWhos(_nun), _nHim = setup.pronounceWho(_nun)>>
<<set _couple = setup.npc.areMarriedToEachOther(_a, _b)>>
<<set _aMc = setup.npc.mcName(_a), _bMc = setup.npc.mcName(_b), _nMc = setup.npc.mcName(_nun)>>

You come in to find <<=_aName>> and <<=_bName>> on opposite ends of a bench, both pointedly studying the floor, with <<=_nunName>> kneeling on the boards in front of them and holding one of each of their hands.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _a>>
	<<if _couple>>
		I just want to feel like my <<=_b.gender === 1 ? 'husband' : 'wife'>> actually sees me. Is that too much?
	<<else>>
		I thought we had something. Then <<=setup.pronounceWhat(_b)>> spends the whole evening laughing with everyone else and barely looks at me.
	<</if>>
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<sayNpc _b>>
	Because every time I do, you look away first! How am I supposed to know what you want?
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<sayNpc _nun>>
	Do you hear that? You're both afraid of the same thing. The holy texts tell us that love is a door you have to open from your own side. Neither of you can do it for the other. But you can both reach for the handle at the same time.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />
<<=_nunName>> glances over at you, a little flushed, as if <<=_nHe>> isn't sure whether <<=_nHe>> has said too much or not quite enough.
<br /><br />
<<sayNpc _b>>
	Oh, good, <<=_bMc>> is here. Now everyone gets to watch.
<</sayNpc>>
<br />

<div id="ce_choices">
	<<link `'Let ' + _nHim + ' guide them'`>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<addmins 5>>
			<<sayNpc _nun>>
				Let me try, <<=_nMc>>. I think they're closer than they look.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<if setup.percentageChance(_ce.reconcileChance(_nun))>>
				<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _a, 'happy', 1, 2)>>
				<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _b, 'happy', 1, 2)>>
				<<run _ce.betweenByNun(_nun, _a, _b, 1, 2)>>
				<<run _fx.changeBetween(_a, _nun, 1, 2)>>
				<<run _fx.changeBetween(_b, _nun, 1, 2)>>
				You hang back and let <<=_nunName>> work. It doesn't take long. <<=_bName>> says something too quiet for you to hear, <<=_aName>> finally looks up, and then they are both talking at once, apologising over each other.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _nun>>
					There. Now, don't let it go cold again. Words are a start, but the body remembers things the mind forgets. Go and remind each other.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				<<if _ce.pairOk(_a, _b)>>
					<<set _trio = [_a, _b, _nun]>>
					<<set _nunJoins = _ce.pairOk(_nun, _a, _nun) && _ce.pairOk(_nun, _b, _nun) && !!_ce.guestScene(_trio) && setup.percentageChance(50)>>
					<<set _together = _nunJoins ? _trio : [_a, _b]>>
					<<set _scene = _ce.guestScene(_together)>>
					<<if _scene>>
						<<if _nunJoins>>
							<<if _ce.nunYields(_nun, [_a, _b])>><<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _nun, 'sub', 1, 2)>><</if>>
							<<=_aName>> takes <<=_bName>> by the hand and pulls <<=setup.pronounceWho(_b)>> toward the dormitory. At the door, <<=_bName>> looks back and holds out <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_b)>> other hand to <<=_nunName>>, and after only a moment's hesitation, <<=_nHe>> takes it.
						<<else>>
							<<=_aName>> takes <<=_bName>> by the hand and pulls <<=setup.pronounceWho(_b)>> toward the dormitory. <<=_nunName>> watches them go with a soft, satisfied smile.
						<</if>>
						<br /><br />
						<div id="ce_after">
							<<ceWatchLinks _scene _together>>
							<<nurseryEffects>>
						</div>
					<<else>>
						They leave arm in arm, heads bent close together.
						<br /><br />
						[[Continue|Guest house]]
						<<nurseryEffects>>
					<</if>>
				<<else>>
					They don't go quite as far as <<=_nunName>> would like, but they leave sitting close, their knees touching, and that is something.
					<br /><br />
					[[Continue|Guest house]]
					<<nurseryEffects>>
				<</if>>
			<<else>>
				You hang back and let <<=_nunName>> work, but this one is too raw. <<=_bName>> gets up first, then <<=_aName>>, and they go off in different directions. <<=_nunName>> sits back on <<=_nHis>> heels and lets out a long sigh.
				<br /><br />
				<<sayNpc _nun>>
					Not today, then. But the door is still there.
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				[[Continue|Guest house]]
				<<nurseryEffects>>
			<</if>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
	<<for _side range [_a, _b]>>
		<<capture _side>>
			<<set _sideLabel = 'Side with ' + setup.displayName(_side)>>
			<<link _sideLabel>>
				<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
					<<addmins 10>>
					<<set _other = _side === _a ? _b : _a>>
					<<set _sName = setup.displayName(_side)>>
					<<run _fx.change(_side, 'happy', 1, 3)>>
					<<run _fx.change(_side, 'relationship', 2, 4)>>
					You tell them how it looks from where you're standing, and how it looks is that <<=_sName>> has a point. <<=setup.displayName(_other)>> throws up <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_other)>> hands and stalks off. <<=_nunName>> sighs and goes after <<=setup.pronounceWho(_other)>>, and <<=_sName>> is left on the bench, looking up at you with something warm and grateful in <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_side)>> eyes.
					<br /><br />
					<<if _ce.mcOk(_side)>>
						<<sayNpc _side>>
							Thank you for being on my side, <<=setup.npc.mcName(_side)>>. Nobody else ever is. Let me thank you properly?
						<</sayNpc>>
						<br />
						<<set _blocked = _ce.mcBlockedBy()>>
						<<set _thanksLabel = 'Let ' + setup.pronounceWho(_side) + ' thank you'>>
						<<if _blocked>>
							<div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc"><<=_thanksLabel>> (<<=_blocked>>)</div>
						<<else>>
							<<set _sideOnly = [_side]>>
							<<ceSexLink _thanksLabel 'solo' _sideOnly>>
						<</if>>
						[[Leave it at that|Guest house]]
						<<nurseryEffects>>
					<<else>>
						<<sayNpc _side>>
							Thank you, <<=setup.npc.mcName(_side)>>. It means a lot that somebody sees it my way.
						<</sayNpc>>
						<br />
						[[Continue|Guest house]]
						<<nurseryEffects>>
					<</if>>
				<</replace>>
			<</link>>
		<</capture>>
	<</for>>
	<<link `'Help ' + _nHim + ' bring them back together (Uses 30 minutes)'`>>
		<<replace '#ce_choices'>>
			<<addmins 30>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _a, 'happy', 2, 4)>>
			<<run _ce.byNun(_nun, _b, 'happy', 2, 4)>>
			<<run _ce.betweenByNun(_nun, _a, _b, 3, 5)>>
			<<run _fx.changeBetween(_a, _nun, 2, 4)>>
			<<run _fx.changeBetween(_b, _nun, 2, 4)>>
			<<run [_a, _b, _nun].forEach(npc => _fx.change(npc, 'relationship', 3, 5))>>
			You crouch down beside <<=_nunName>>. Between the two of you, you coax it out of them: the small hurts, the things each of them wanted to say and didn't. You make <<=_aName>> say the kind thing first, and <<=_bName>> has to bite <<=setup.pronounceWhos(_b)>> lip to keep from smiling.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _a>>
				Alright, alright, <<=_aMc>>. I'm saying it. I missed you, okay?
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			<<=_nunName>> lays their joined hands together in <<=_nHis>> lap and closes <<=_nHis>> eyes.
			<br /><br />
			<<sayNpc _nun>>
				Bless what has been mended here. Let it grow stronger where it was broken.
			<</sayNpc>>
			<br />
			When <<=_nHe>> opens <<=_nHis>> eyes again, <<=_aName>> and <<=_bName>> are looking at each other the way they clearly wanted to all along, and then, together, they look at you.
			<br /><br />
			<<set _pair = _ce.threesome(_a, _b)>>
			<<set _four = [_a, _b, _nun]>>
			<<set _fourOk = _ce.foursomeOk(_four)>>
			<<if _pair || _fourOk>>
				<<sayNpc _nun>>
					They want to thank you. And to celebrate. I think love this new should be shared, don't you?
				<</sayNpc>>
				<br />
				<<set _blocked = _ce.mcBlockedBy()>>
				<<if _blocked>>
					<<if _pair>><div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc">Celebrate with them both (<<=_blocked>>)</div><</if>>
					<<if _fourOk>><div class="link-internal" style="background: #ccc">Celebrate with all three of them (<<=_blocked>>)</div><</if>>
				<<else>>
					<<if _pair>>
						<<ceSexLink 'Celebrate with them both' 'threesome' _pair>>
					<</if>>
					<<if _fourOk>>
						<<set _fourLabel = 'Celebrate with all three of them, ' + _nunName + ' included'>>
						<<set _fourChanges = _ce.nunYields(_nun, [_a, _b]) ? _ce.byNunChanges(_nun, [{ npc: _nun, stat: 'sub', low: 1, high: 2 }]) : []>>
						<<ceSexLink _fourLabel 'foursome' _four _fourChanges>>
					<</if>>
				<</if>>
				[[Let them celebrate on their own|Guest house]]
				<<nurseryEffects>>
			<<else>>
				[[Continue|Guest house]]
				<<nurseryEffects>>
			<</if>>
		<</replace>>
	<</link>>
</div>
<</if>>
